.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509V3_SET_CTX 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509V3_set_ctx ,
.Nm X509V3_set_issuer_pkey
.Nd X.509 v3 extension generation utilities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509v3.h
.Ft void
.Fo X509V3_set_ctx
.Fa "X509V3_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "X509 *issuer"
.Fa "X509 *subject"
.Fa "X509_REQ *req"
.Fa "X509_CRL *crl"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509V3_set_issuer_pkey
.Fa "X509V3_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509V3_set_ctx
fills in the basic fields of
.Fa ctx
of type
.Vt X509V3_CTX ,
providing details potentially needed by functions producing X509 v3
extensions.
These may make use of fields of the certificate
.Fa subject ,
the certification request
.Fa req ,
or the certificate revocation list
.Fa crl .
At most one of these three parameters can be non-NULL. When constructing
the subject key identifier of a certificate by computing a hash value of
its public key, the public key is taken from
.Fa subject
or
.Fa req .
Similarly, when constructing subject alternative names from any email
addresses contained in a subject DN, the subject DN is taken from
.Fa subject
or
.Fa req .
If
.Fa subject
or
.Fa crl
is provided,
.Fa issuer
should point to its issuer, for instance as a reference for generating
the authority key identifier extension.
.Fa issuer
may be the same pointer value as
.Fa subject
(which usually is an indication that the
.Fa subject
certificate is self-issued or even self-signed).
In this case the fallback source for generating the authority key
identifier extension will be taken from any value provided using
.Fn X509V3_set_issuer_pkey .
.Fa flags
may be 0 or contain
.Sy X509V3_CTX_TEST ,
which means that just the syntax of extension definitions is to be
checked without actually producing any extension, or
.Sy X509V3_CTX_REPLACE ,
which means that each X.509v3 extension added as defined in some
configuration section shall replace any already existing extension with
the same OID.
.Pp
.Fn X509V3_set_issuer_pkey
explicitly sets the issuer private key of the subject certificate that
has been provided in
.Fa ctx .
This should be done in case the
.Fa issuer
and
.Fa subject
arguments to
.Fn X509V3_set_ctx
have the same pointer value to provide fallback data for the authority
key identifier extension.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509V3_set_issuer_pkey
returns 1 on success and 0 on error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr X509_add_ext 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn X509V3_set_issuer_pkey
was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
CTX_TEST was deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0; use X509V3_CTX_TEST instead.
